"""
GB_ETYS_Eunice2022 -- GB transmission network, storm window 2022-02-18 00:00:00 to 2022-02-19 00:00:00 (25 hourly snapshots)

Built from PyPSA-GB: ETYS 2022 Appendix B topology (buses, lines, transformers, ratings), DUKES/REPD fleet,
ERA5 wind and solar availability, ESPENI demand split to GSPs.  See README_network_inputs.md.

Differences from a stock case:
    - 2023 buses (7 external HVDC terminals and the Caithness-Moray DC midpoint dropped)
    - 3021 branches: 0 lines, 1445 transformers,
      2 internal HVDC links as equivalent AC branches (Western Link, Caithness-Moray)
    - 3509 units: 3418 generators on by default; storage and interconnectors listed, off by default
    - Pmin = 0 for every unit; Pmax = p_nom x availability(t), Pg = 0 (dispatch left to the DC OPF)
    - gencost linear: c1 = PyPSA-GB marginal cost (GBP/MWh), no tie-break; no load shedding (use load2disp)

Usage:
    from GB_ETYS_Eunice2022 import GB_ETYS_Eunice2022 as load_case
    ppc = load_case()                         # hour 0
    ppc = load_case(h=12)                     # hour index 0..24, see ppc['snapshot']
    ppc = load_case(h=12, include=('generator', 'storage'))   # storage on as fast reserve
"""

